WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Statutory Sick Pay (SSP): if you are an employee and ill for at least one full working day, your employer pays you up to £123.25 a week for up to 28 weeks. Your contract may give you more.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:31.300
Tell your employer as soon as possible, as your contract says. If you are off for more than 7 days in a row, you will usually be asked for a «fit note» from your GP.

3
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:47.300
Holidays: if you work 5 days a week, you get at least 28 paid days a year (5.6 weeks). Your employer can include bank holidays in them. If you work fewer days, you get a proportional share.

4
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:54.100
If you are not paid what you are owed, Acas gives free advice.

5
00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:59.100
Say it aloud: “I'm off sick today.”.
